## 14. LIVE release gates (all required)

Do not mark LIVE-ready unless all are true and evidenced:

- Binance rules and adapter behavior are checked against current official docs and Testnet where possible;
- `TEST` architecture cannot call any real order mutation method, and this is covered by tests;
- LIVE is disabled by default, separate credentials, least privilege, explicit local activation and risk confirmation;
- account snapshot, symbol filters, position mode, open orders/positions and reconciliation are all healthy and fresh before new grid;
- all allocation, margin, gross/net, drawdown, per-symbol, daily-loss, open-order and funding limits are explicitly configured and hard-enforced; if a required limit is absent, block LIVE;
- no external/unowned position or order is silently adopted/closed;
- both simultaneous grids fit their combined worst-case scenario; no simplistic liquidation formula is used as risk proof;
- order idempotency, timeout reconciliation, partial fills, close semantics and shutdown/restart are tested;
- emergency/stop policy, Windows offline behavior, Telegram relay and security are documented;
- user explicitly understands fees, funding, slippage, liquidation, maker non-fill, machine downtime and risk of loss.

Passing tests does not prove strategy profitability or eliminate operational risk. LIVE activation remains a separate user decision.

